From d60f985815f137e1c6ada02888686e039163bfe1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 09:02:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Make resumed conversations available during skill discovery

Run owned startup skill discovery without delaying session availability.
History restoration captures model metadata without skill discovery. Execution
waits for the shared warmup and keeps configuration-specific discovery.

Cold client resumes register skill watches in the listener background. After
watch installation and response/snapshot publication, refresh metadata so
changes during registration cannot leave clients with a stale catalog. New
sessions and forks retain synchronous watches and their response ordering.
Late registrations cannot outlive a replaced or closed listener.

Base: rust-v0.160.0 a956835d020762cb2b570053af06f643a11c0ecc.
TDD receipts: workspace .cat/work/reports/resume-background/. Three initial
restoration checks fail against base; six lifecycle checks pass with warmup.
Existing watch-change check fails with blanket deferred registration. The new
cold_resume_refreshes_skill_metadata_after_watches_are_ready check times out
for its missing refresh (watch-readiness-red-2.log). After correcting startup
policy, focused watch, publication-order, and lifecycle checks pass 6/6
(watch-readiness-green-2.log). Author just fmt-check passes.
This intermediate source snapshot requires final emitted-patch and native gates.
